  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:4975",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the targeting of A2058 through multiple indirect pathways, with the most direct link emerging from the interaction with P2X purinoceptor 1. This receptor is targeted by Mollicellin N, which in turn influences A2058. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin may act through a series of molecular intermediates, ultimately affecting A2058 via the P2X purinoceptor pathway. Complementary evidence from other paths points to a shared target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which also targets A2058, indicating a potential role for this compound in the pathway. The integration of these findings highlights a possible mechanism where doxorubicin indirectly modulates A2058 through a network of targets, emphasizing the complexity of its interaction with cellular processes.",
